#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203797 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d6226fdb-ee73-5a78-87d5-9d6a988a9eb4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation With No Solutions"}] :question/id #uuid "fd07ad0f-548a-5569-84de-d658a88c4b9c" :question/math-academy-id "e-17087" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\n1. $4z + 3 = 4z + 9$\n2. $2z - 5 = z + 1$\n3. $3z - 2 = 3z - 2$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n$4z + 3|= 4z + 9; 4z + 3 - 4z|= 4z + 9 - 4z; 3|= 9$.\nThis equation is false for all values of $z$. Therefore, the equation $4z + 3 = 4z + 9$ has no solutions.\n- For the second equation, we have\n$2z - 5|= z + 1; 2z - 5 - z + 5|= z + 1 - z + 5; z|= 6$.\nTherefore, the equation $2z - 5 = z + 1$ has the unique solution $z = 6$.\n- For the third equation, we have\n$3z - 2|= 3z - 2; 3z - 2 - 3z|= 3z - 2 - 3z; - 2|=-2$.\nThis equation is true for all values of $z$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203798 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e7426e-553d-5f20-811f-15f3a5ea0056" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter"}] :question/id #uuid "cba9196c-fdc3-594d-a1ad-948cf75bd366" :question/math-academy-id "e-17213" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $y$, given by\n$4(r - 2)y = -8$\nwhere $r$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $r$?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n$ax = b$\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and\n\n$$\nb\\neq 0\n$$\n\nIf $a = 0$, then the equation has no solution.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ay = b$. In this case,\n\n$$\na = 4(r - 2), \\qquad b = -8\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n4(r - 2) = 0\n$$\n\nSolving this for $r$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4(r - 2) &= 0 \\\\\n(4(r - 2))/(4) &= \\frac{0}{4} \\\\\nr - 2 &= 0 \\\\\nr &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203799 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Variables and Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/id #uuid "36eadc0b-c2b0-5f84-8f39-2b8399932edb" :question/math-academy-id "e-17214" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $x$, given by\n$2nx + 7 = -4x + 5$\nwhere $n$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $n$?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n$ax = b$\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and\n\n$$\nb\\neq 0\n$$\n\nIf $a = 0$, then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $ax = b$.\n\nWe start by adding $4x$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2nx + 7 &= -4x + 5 \\\\\n2nx + 4x + 7 &= -4x + 5 + 4x \\\\\n2nx + 4x + 7 &= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we subtract $7$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2nx + 4x + 7 &= 5 \\\\\n2nx + 4x + 7 - 7 &= 5 - 7 \\\\\n2nx + 4x &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $x$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(2n + 4)x = -2\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $ax = b{:}$\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{(2n + 4)}_{a}x = \\underbrace{-2}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n2n + 4= 0\n$$\n\nSolving this for $n$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2n + 4 &= 0 \\\\\n2n + 4 - 4 &= 0 - 4 \\\\\n2n &= -4 \\\\\n\\frac{2n}{2} &= \\frac{-4}{2} \\\\\nn &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203820 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba644b27-7245-5b7b-8cd6-2493836a7d03" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/id #uuid "5ee14499-89b0-59a3-9f13-b0a00c0e518d" :question/math-academy-id "e-18853" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $z$, given by\n$(r - 9)z + 2 = -1$\nwhere $r$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $r$?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n$ax = b$\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and\n\n$$\nb\\neq 0\n$$\n\nIf $a = 0$, then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $az = b{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(r - 9)z + 2 &= -1 \\\\\n(r - 9)z + 2 - 2 &= -1 - 2 \\\\\n(r - 9)_(⏟)_(a)z &= -3_(⏟)_(b)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n$r - 9 = 0$.\n\nSolving this for $r$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr - 9 &= 0 \\\\\nr &= 9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204539 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba644b27-7245-5b7b-8cd6-2493836a7d03" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1afe64ee-6a95-55d0-ae94-eebb04a6359d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1afe64ee-6a95-55d0-ae94-eebb04a6359d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232435} :answer-field/id #uuid "871f23cd-6756-596d-8c73-99acd164790c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203438}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "38670cb7-04d7-5bd3-bbc0-32b596369870" :question/math-academy-id "q-287667" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $x$, given by\n$2(p - 4)x + 2 = 5$\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p$?$p =$\n{{field-1}}\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"solving-for-an-unknown-parameter-variables-and-constants-on-both-sides\"></a>" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(p-4)x+2 & =5 \\\\ 2(p-4)x+2-2 & =5-2 \\\\ {{2(p-4)}_{⏟}}_{a}x & ={{3}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n2(p-4)=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(p-4) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(p-4)}{2} & =\\frac{0}{2} \\\\ p-4 & =0 \\\\ p & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252921 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d6226fdb-ee73-5a78-87d5-9d6a988a9eb4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation With No Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89e4cb7d-e084-50ea-b6cd-64ffcfd56732" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252923} {:answer/id #uuid "77caee0e-cb2b-545e-a1c7-e34029d79d1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252924} {:answer/id #uuid "341e2d03-3d2f-5bb8-bd37-c072e48341cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252925} {:answer/id #uuid "dcd7a74d-e8d3-5f1d-8990-4a9cefa408e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252926} {:answer/id #uuid "7d71a477-c8e9-5ea1-bff2-f85b4b744d23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d71a477-c8e9-5ea1-bff2-f85b4b744d23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252927} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a2c1e03-713c-5b0e-be8d-12842f0f5344" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252922}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9ac74280-e3d7-5ecf-bd93-b4a85d630d51" :question/math-academy-id "q-288066" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\n- $-3u+4=-3u-1$\n- $2u+5=2u+8$\n- $6u-2=3u+1$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3u+4 & =-3u-1 \\\\ -3u+4+3u & =-3u-1+3u \\\\ 4 & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $u.$ Therefore, the equation $-3u+4=-3u-1$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2u+5 & =2u+8 \\\\ 2u+5-2u & =2u+8-2u \\\\ 5 & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $u.$ Therefore, the equation $2u+5=2u+8$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6u-2 & =3u+1 \\\\ 6u-2-3u+2 & =3u+1-3u+2 \\\\ 3u & =3 \\\\ u & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $6u-2=3u+1$ has the unique solution $u=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252928 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d6226fdb-ee73-5a78-87d5-9d6a988a9eb4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation With No Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c708be9e-ad93-519a-a3ec-fe6426e02b11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252930} {:answer/id #uuid "6621e02e-818e-5ffd-aad1-abbc6bdb2482" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252931} {:answer/id #uuid "dddd2ac9-fd00-5018-91f7-c30dc727cdbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252932} {:answer/id #uuid "f0dacd0f-b074-5fc6-866e-77c81600fa49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252933} {:answer/id #uuid "d0cc680e-3862-5741-a6ba-91aa86abef8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252934}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0cc680e-3862-5741-a6ba-91aa86abef8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252934} :answer-field/id #uuid "c12deb50-4da8-53eb-9edf-73092abbf67c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252929}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f5a6b09f-75cb-52e3-a292-011882596ba1" :question/math-academy-id "q-288070" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\n- $-4y+2=-4y-5$\n- $6y+3=6y-1$\n- $5y-7=2y+1$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4y+2 & =-4y-5 \\\\ -4y+2+4y & =-4y-5+4y \\\\ 2 & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $y.$ Therefore, the equation $-4y+2=-4y-5$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6y+3 & =6y-1 \\\\ 6y+3-6y & =6y-1-6y \\\\ 3 & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $y.$ Therefore, the equation $6y+3=6y-1$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5y-7 & =2y+1 \\\\ 5y-7-2y+7 & =2y+1-2y+7 \\\\ 3y & =8 \\\\ y & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $5y-7=2y+1$ has the unique solution $y=\\frac{8}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252935 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d6226fdb-ee73-5a78-87d5-9d6a988a9eb4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation With No Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6adea89-d41b-5597-ae70-6431ee6bb61d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252937} {:answer/id #uuid "f241a01d-944a-5a8f-a2d2-d043c2b9c572" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252938} {:answer/id #uuid "5ba8d8e0-4f2f-5336-8ec3-784f679e6e86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252939} {:answer/id #uuid "cf8c6733-04d9-57c0-8af4-6f8908e87637" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252940} {:answer/id #uuid "1a6f6fa6-a654-57d5-a5af-dc3cf27dcd90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ba8d8e0-4f2f-5336-8ec3-784f679e6e86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252939} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5d66a6e-390d-5e39-9f81-465c75bd6cb8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252936}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6565f488-1011-5578-9815-562b58af2063" :question/math-academy-id "q-288072" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\n- $2z-4=2z+1$\n- $5z+6=5z+6$\n- $3z+2=z+4$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2z-4 & =2z+1 \\\\ 2z-4-2z & =2z+1-2z \\\\ -4 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $z.$ Therefore, the equation $2z-4=2z+1$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5z+6 & =5z+6 \\\\ 5z+6-5z & =5z+6-5z \\\\ 6 & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $z.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3z+2 & =z+4 \\\\ 3z+2-z-2 & =z+4-z-2 \\\\ 2z & =2 \\\\ z & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $3z+2=z+4$ has the unique solution $z=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252942 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d6226fdb-ee73-5a78-87d5-9d6a988a9eb4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation With No Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b607b456-4991-5d86-a098-c4454d7e1413" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252944} {:answer/id #uuid "f469b62c-2346-5224-bb32-6b7202220c47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252945} {:answer/id #uuid "85d39552-b417-5896-a2ff-27880f2e02e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252946} {:answer/id #uuid "5a5484a5-80d8-533c-8bc1-e123b4760180" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252947} {:answer/id #uuid "45abebeb-486a-516c-bb41-0c48f3a3a363" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252948}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a5484a5-80d8-533c-8bc1-e123b4760180" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252947} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb6c2fda-38a0-5aa3-bfa5-43be6ad691f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252943}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "753a11b9-6734-56f2-9436-eb016d3b96ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-288073" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\n- $3w+2=2w+2$\n- $4w-7=4w-7$\n- $6w+5=6w+9$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3w+2 & =2w+2 \\\\ 3w+2-2w-2 & =2w+2-2w-2 \\\\ w & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $3w+2=2w+2$ has the unique solution $w=0.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4w-7 & =4w-7 \\\\ 4w-7-4w & =4w-7-4w \\\\ -7 & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $w.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6w+5 & =6w+9 \\\\ 6w+5-6w & =6w+9-6w \\\\ 5 & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $w.$ Therefore, the equation $6w+5=6w+9$ has no solutions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252949 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d6226fdb-ee73-5a78-87d5-9d6a988a9eb4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation With No Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ecd7dd2-a79f-5074-a90b-90e1cd0828ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252951} {:answer/id #uuid "be4e378e-e746-52e6-905b-a149718dfe7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252952} {:answer/id #uuid "4d622349-4f7f-56d4-86c4-dbd1339f62f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252953} {:answer/id #uuid "d35c75d2-56f0-5417-aa37-6dd7a90446d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252954} {:answer/id #uuid "c1c9f0ed-a6e9-5ee4-9717-d975fc12e979" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252955}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1c9f0ed-a6e9-5ee4-9717-d975fc12e979" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252955} :answer-field/id #uuid "8beaca44-1c22-5d4b-bb33-f44c5ffa7036" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252950}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b7570f56-19aa-5f26-9c89-32b984a0d42a" :question/math-academy-id "q-288074" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\n- $9v-5=4v+2$\n- $2v+3=2v+7$\n- $5v-1=5v-1$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9v-5 & =4v+2 \\\\ 9v-5-4v+5 & =4v+2-4v+5 \\\\ 5v & =7 \\\\ v & =\\frac{7}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $9v-5=4v+2$ has the unique solution $v=\\frac{7}{5}.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2v+3 & =2v+7 \\\\ 2v+3-2v & =2v+7-2v \\\\ 3 & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $v.$ Therefore, the equation $2v+3=2v+7$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5v-1 & =5v-1 \\\\ 5v-1-5v & =5v-1-5v \\\\ -1 & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $v.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252956 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e7426e-553d-5f20-811f-15f3a5ea0056" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1ea1cf4-7015-57df-9a73-3b7aaf871ead" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252958} {:answer/id #uuid "cf3fb9e0-270e-573a-b102-f8d121ce7af0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252959} {:answer/id #uuid "0c017dfa-885a-540c-b1c9-9c0893c40a79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252960} {:answer/id #uuid "00a38c29-6b42-5ffd-aee1-db689452d9a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252961} {:answer/id #uuid "3adffc9e-0a52-50d6-a0ef-a4adb6067037" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c017dfa-885a-540c-b1c9-9c0893c40a79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252960} :answer-field/id #uuid "7af9d979-bbbb-573d-8e20-46cd41193e03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252957}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c509c032-41c2-54c1-84a0-f41c2fd89b3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-288135" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $y,$ given by\n\n$$\n4py=-2\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ay=b.$ In this case,\n\n$$\na=4p,\\,b=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n4p=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\np=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252963 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e7426e-553d-5f20-811f-15f3a5ea0056" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "baaa7d9f-020c-53e3-93fd-ae8f54167939" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252965} {:answer/id #uuid "7e2dc77d-82d9-5fd4-b4c2-40d4cd1d52a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252966} {:answer/id #uuid "a03d5388-f830-50d0-bc5a-00b2720c23dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252967} {:answer/id #uuid "b8d87cf6-efa2-5d63-8fc7-f5ed865f3cc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252968} {:answer/id #uuid "f6f9c63a-2de4-5b99-b961-652607dfc5e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252969}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e2dc77d-82d9-5fd4-b4c2-40d4cd1d52a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252966} :answer-field/id #uuid "f465b249-9525-5de4-9ed8-e182f2bc66f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252964}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7eee3c83-0bc4-553e-96c8-f6ecedccf2d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-288143" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $x,$ given by\n\n$$\n-3(q+4)x=6\n$$\n\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $q?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=b.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=-3(q+4),\\,b=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n-3(q+4)=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3(q+4) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{-3(q+4)}{-3} & =\\frac{0}{-3} \\\\ q+4 & =0 \\\\ q & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252970 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e7426e-553d-5f20-811f-15f3a5ea0056" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "422f0c92-53fe-51bb-9892-289721abbb4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252972} {:answer/id #uuid "2366889c-af5d-5743-8e6d-161f4a222a77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252973} {:answer/id #uuid "f28f3b67-3822-51ec-8ab2-51729b671cad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252974} {:answer/id #uuid "017d2336-5c59-523b-ba15-5ef9d7e3b88a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252975} {:answer/id #uuid "3e5e61ef-b29c-5f19-898f-57ee3b98e087" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "422f0c92-53fe-51bb-9892-289721abbb4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252972} :answer-field/id #uuid "a71de821-baaf-5ed2-a1d9-25db8737a220" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252971}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d9d87fe6-b6e0-5ddd-bc49-0e873da45bf9" :question/math-academy-id "q-288144" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $z,$ given by\n\n$$\n-5(p-9)z=10\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $az=b.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=-5(p-9),\\,b=10.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n-5(p-9)=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5(p-9) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{-5(p-9)}{-5} & =\\frac{0}{-5} \\\\ p-9 & =0 \\\\ p & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204544 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e7426e-553d-5f20-811f-15f3a5ea0056" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0b2e78a-6e20-549c-bc9b-892664180c32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203459} {:answer/id #uuid "d9d04615-1d41-5a45-ba9b-8ba79bb5ff41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203460} {:answer/id #uuid "fb9e3819-10ff-5567-a85b-bddce1db025c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203461} {:answer/id #uuid "2e74dea8-50dc-55e4-b514-bbcd47a4907c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203462} {:answer/id #uuid "55315068-5d60-51ae-a190-c7d4dbfb8e29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9d04615-1d41-5a45-ba9b-8ba79bb5ff41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203460} :answer-field/id #uuid "4594c658-f6ef-5788-bb0b-f1d8af9ae065" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203458}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "328a41df-8074-5d3e-9600-d58da9a2fa99" :question/math-academy-id "q-288593" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $y$, given by\n\n$(q - 1)y = 4$\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $q$?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ay=b.$ In this case,\n\n$$\na=q-1,\\,b=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\nq-1=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q-1 & =0 \\\\ q & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252977 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e7426e-553d-5f20-811f-15f3a5ea0056" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6c7bac6-6a29-5343-8521-62c1fd35b7e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252979} {:answer/id #uuid "a4a9777c-c4a1-5e3e-a0e7-e8c456717ab8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252980} {:answer/id #uuid "c0f277d2-9e6f-52d6-b109-0df2021c60a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252981} {:answer/id #uuid "3ef0d44e-2bb6-53df-b130-55819d6b5206" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252982} {:answer/id #uuid "6b15d697-6be4-5e0f-bfca-6a35d0a2ff3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6c7bac6-6a29-5343-8521-62c1fd35b7e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252979} :answer-field/id #uuid "03c94371-0161-53f1-bc55-d8fb98c94d58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252978}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f39c29af-4dc2-56e4-9621-65072963367d" :question/math-academy-id "q-288596" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $y,$ given by\n\n$$\n(q+9)y=-6\n$$\n\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $q?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ay=b.$ In this case,\n\n$$\na=q+9,\\,b=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\nq+9=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q+9 & =0 \\\\ q & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252984 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba644b27-7245-5b7b-8cd6-2493836a7d03" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24d10d47-f933-561e-af9e-138002f6c5b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24d10d47-f933-561e-af9e-138002f6c5b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252986} :answer-field/id #uuid "db24cc88-516f-5f07-8fef-8e2dc0303186" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252985}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4bf47b67-ad18-5292-b32f-954004aeb3fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-288634" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $x,$ given by\n\n$$\n3(p+2)x+7=10\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(p+2)x+7 & =10 \\\\ 3(p+2)x+7-7 & =10-7 \\\\ {{3(p+2)}_{⏟}}_{a}x & ={{3}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n3(p+2)=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(p+2) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3(p+2)}{3} & =\\frac{0}{3} \\\\ p+2 & =0 \\\\ p & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252987 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba644b27-7245-5b7b-8cd6-2493836a7d03" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e26f11a-958e-573c-8fc9-e3595a06e50f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252989} {:answer/id #uuid "39d860c2-c6b2-5646-821c-92bb62d8c2a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252990}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e26f11a-958e-573c-8fc9-e3595a06e50f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252989} :answer-field/id #uuid "76181339-5cd7-5650-b143-bb2c8db6135d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252988}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9021d130-3d7b-513a-93e6-cae05d8662af" :question/math-academy-id "q-288644" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $v,$ given by\n\n$$\n(k-2)v-3=5\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $k?$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $av=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(k-2)v-3 & =5 \\\\ (k-2)v-3+3 & =5+3 \\\\ {{(k-2)}_{⏟}}_{a}v & ={{8}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\nk-2=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k-2 & =0 \\\\ k & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252991 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba644b27-7245-5b7b-8cd6-2493836a7d03" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "390874bc-bfd8-578c-90b5-a69ca89dfaed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "390874bc-bfd8-578c-90b5-a69ca89dfaed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252993} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c50eb8a-ba2d-559e-9d3b-3ecc0ed9a818" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252992}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d6f2f316-a4ef-51a7-99f1-5d44fefeac54" :question/math-academy-id "q-288646" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $x,$ given by\n\n$$\n(m+6)x+2=7\n$$\n\nwhere $m$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $m?$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(m+6)x+2 & =7 \\\\ (m+6)x+2-2 & =7-2 \\\\ {{(m+6)}_{⏟}}_{a}x & ={{5}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\nm+6=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $m,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m+6 & =0 \\\\ m & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252994 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba644b27-7245-5b7b-8cd6-2493836a7d03" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "655c1563-4247-5421-aad0-8de8729e158f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252996} {:answer/id #uuid "ae7582f2-02b5-5d13-969e-f059e51cfb49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252997}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae7582f2-02b5-5d13-969e-f059e51cfb49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252997} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecde7c59-4b71-5d7f-9e56-2edb8d2fa1cb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252995}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e5aeefd8-dd0b-554b-bac9-09059b0855e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-288648" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $u,$ given by\n\n$$\n(q-5)u+9=0\n$$\n\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $q?$\n\n$q=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $au=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(q-5)u+9 & =0 \\\\ (q-5)u+9-9 & =0-9 \\\\ {{(q-5)}_{⏟}}_{a}u & ={{-9}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\nq-5=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q-5 & =0 \\\\ q & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252998 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Variables and Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8a86eb1-d43c-52b0-8a83-3f4b2861b4f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253000} {:answer/id #uuid "3df5b0de-5ab5-57e4-949b-8a019f9a7fe6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253001} {:answer/id #uuid "45166757-4947-5d25-afe0-cb04e8d26352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253002} {:answer/id #uuid "c8b1b9c0-a2e5-54d6-8ca2-b1cc23935b23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253003} {:answer/id #uuid "4a668c7e-53b0-5fdc-9fd6-7a96bf353f7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253004}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8b1b9c0-a2e5-54d6-8ca2-b1cc23935b23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253003} :answer-field/id #uuid "e70af324-e6b8-5133-9ebf-4d27f28209f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252999}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "65b5657a-e041-5dba-9476-47eab2ebbed2" :question/math-academy-id "q-288662" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $y,$ given by\n\n$$\n3py=5y+8\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $ay=b.$ \n\nWe start by subtracting $5y$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3py & =5y+8 \\\\ 3py-5y & =5y+8-5y \\\\ 3py-5y & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $y$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(3p-5)y=8.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $ay=b:$\n\n$$\n{{(3p-5)}_{⏟}}_{a}y={{8}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n3p-5=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3p-5 & =0 \\\\ 3p-5+5 & =0+5 \\\\ 3p & =5 \\\\ \\frac{3p}{3} & =\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ p & =\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253005 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Variables and Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dce29a62-1b39-597a-a127-fc69af7bfb2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253007} {:answer/id #uuid "94f07611-43e2-5403-ae2e-311a95f08b08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253008}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dce29a62-1b39-597a-a127-fc69af7bfb2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253007} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0b495d4-9421-58a5-a258-9fce37cad603" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253006}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "29b2eed1-2fce-5eb7-8c1b-247497813df5" :question/math-academy-id "q-288673" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $z,$ given by\n\n$$\n3qz+4=7z+1\n$$\n\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $q?$\n\n$q=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $az=b.$ \n\nWe start by subtracting $7z$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3qz+4 & =7z+1 \\\\ 3qz-7z+4 & =7z+1-7z \\\\ 3qz-7z+4 & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we subtract $4$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3qz-7z+4 & =1 \\\\ 3qz-7z+4-4 & =1-4 \\\\ 3qz-7z & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $z$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(3q-7)z=-3.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $az=b:$\n\n$$\n{{(3q-7)}_{⏟}}_{a}z={{-3}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n3q-7=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3q-7 & =0 \\\\ 3q-7+7 & =0+7 \\\\ 3q & =7 \\\\ \\frac{3q}{3} & =\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ q & =\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253009 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Variables and Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dab68e7c-7769-5198-8881-83b60f206c81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dab68e7c-7769-5198-8881-83b60f206c81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253011} :answer-field/id #uuid "6dc06a7c-b201-563d-838b-13bc201fd4f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253010}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f2f67ac6-2a69-5d98-9eb7-bfa977c1a594" :question/math-academy-id "q-288674" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $u,$ given by\n\n$$\n5ru+3=2u+6\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $r?$\n\n$r=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $au=b.$ \n\nWe start by subtracting $2u$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5ru+3 & =2u+6 \\\\ 5ru-2u+3 & =2u+6-2u \\\\ 5ru-2u+3 & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we subtract $3$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5ru-2u+3 & =6 \\\\ 5ru-2u+3-3 & =6-3 \\\\ 5ru-2u & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $u$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(5r-2)u=3.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $au=b:$\n\n$$\n{{(5r-2)}_{⏟}}_{a}u={{3}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n5r-2=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5r-2 & =0 \\\\ 5r-2+2 & =0+2 \\\\ 5r & =2 \\\\ \\frac{5r}{5} & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ r & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253012 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Variables and Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c5cc0a8-f03b-552a-8e72-3f8d5b2498be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253014} {:answer/id #uuid "a047952d-53ad-53c0-93f8-e21be9834333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253015}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c5cc0a8-f03b-552a-8e72-3f8d5b2498be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253014} :answer-field/id #uuid "201e427b-6e02-5156-8cfe-a29c280f0e79" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253013}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "877e1227-8365-5e43-86f2-3ed7e56a5b5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-288675" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $w,$ given by\n\n$$\n-4mw+5=-3w+1\n$$\n\nwhere $m$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $m?$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $aw=b.$ \n\nWe start by adding $3w$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4mw+5 & =-3w+1 \\\\ -4mw+3w+5 & =-3w+1+3w \\\\ -4mw+3w+5 & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we subtract $5$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4mw+3w+5 & =1 \\\\ -4mw+3w+5-5 & =1-5 \\\\ -4mw+3w & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $w$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(-4m+3)w=-4.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $aw=b:$\n\n$$\n{{(-4m+3)}_{⏟}}_{a}w={{-4}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n-4m+3=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $m,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4m+3 & =0 \\\\ -4m+3-3 & =0-3 \\\\ -4m & =-3 \\\\ \\frac{-4m}{-4} & =\\frac{-3}{-4} \\\\ m & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253016 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Variables and Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bca33de8-9206-5066-b587-df197193ba48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253018}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bca33de8-9206-5066-b587-df197193ba48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253018} :answer-field/id #uuid "68a9b56b-9708-530f-8a62-21763e71626a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253017}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "53621c2d-b714-55a4-bb17-dd8e78db13a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-288678" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $z,$ given by\n\n$$\n-3pz-8=-z-6\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $az=b.$ \n\nWe start by adding $z$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3pz-8 & =-z-6 \\\\ -3pz+z-8 & =-z-6+z \\\\ -3pz+z-8 & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we add $8$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3pz+z-8 & =-6 \\\\ -3pz+z-8+8 & =-6+8 \\\\ -3pz+z & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $z$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(-3p+1)z=2.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $ax=b:$\n\n$$\n{{(-3p+1)}_{⏟}}_{a}z={{2}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n-3p+1=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3p+1 & =0 \\\\ -3p+1-1 & =0-1 \\\\ -3p & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{-3p}{-3} & =\\frac{-1}{-3} \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
